NAME
    theme-check - validate and audit EmuSen Qt/QML theme packages

SYNOPSIS
    theme-check [--static] [--state DIR] <folder>...
    theme-audit [--gpu] [--state DIR] [--states LIST] [--sizes LIST]
                [--crowd with|without|only] [--catalogue FILE]
                [--section KEY] [--focus NAME] [--mockups DIR] <folder>
    theme-audit --list-states

DESCRIPTION
    Command of the emusen.dev module that validates EmuSen Qt/QML theme
    packages (a folder containing theme.json, screens/Home.qml,
    Consoles.qml, Games.qml, optional Splash.qml, parts/, and assets/).
    Validation runs in two stages:

    1. Static check (in-process): verifies theme.json against the schema
       and API version (emusen-theme-manifest), checks referenced asset
       and screen paths, validates token overrides against the committed
       Tokens singleton registry (Testing/qmltypes/EmuSen.Kit-1.13.qmltypes:
       QColor as #RRGGBB/#AARRGGBB, double, int, bool, QString bundled
       font faces, and QVariant two-number dash patterns), verifies WCAG
       2.1 contrast floors (4.5:1 text, 3:1 graphics) for overridden
       token pairs after alpha compositing, and runs qml-rules(1) under
       the sandboxed theme import allow-list (exact matches: QtQuick,
       QtQuick.Layouts, QtQuick.Effects, QtQuick.Shapes,
       QtQuick.Controls, EmuSen.Theme, plus relative package folders).
    2. Loaded audit (theme-audit subprocess): runs only when the static
       stage has no findings (unless --static is passed). Places each
       declared screen in a fresh QML engine through emusen-theme-host
       against a synthetic library (emusen-client-fixture) under the big
       screen form with reduced motion enabled, across every declared
       variant and the five gate sizes (1280x800, 1920x1200, 1920x1080,
       1280x720, 3840x2160).

    Findings print one per line as 'file:line kind words', followed by
    'ok' or 'N findings'. Static finding kinds: schema, api, path,
    screen, token, contrast, note (unknown schema-1 keys, ignored and
    not counted as failures), plus all qml-rules(1) kinds (function,
    callLater, literal, words, onCompleted, rows, import).

    Loaded audit finding kinds (file is the screen path, line 1, with
    size and variant):

        fit         Layout fit violation (clipping, overlap, hard edge
                    without fade, disallowed ellipsis on fixed UI text,
                    overflow, or unreadable text size).
        reach       Operable element unreachable by directional pad walk
                    from initial focus, or console missed by the 120-
                    console crowd sweep.
        pointer     Pointer click at element centre hits another item or
                    fails to invoke A, or wheel fails to scroll a list
                    (not run on Splash).
        chrome      Desktop chrome present in big-screen mode.
        name        Operable element missing an accessible name
                    (Accessible.name or child text).
        contrast    Rendered text below 4.5:1 (3:1 large text) against
                    sampled background pixels behind it. Inactive
                    declined places are exempt only when visibly
                    distinct from their offered state (>= 3:1 change).
                    Mid-transition text under a held clock is skipped.
        exempted    Unruled exemption hit (exemptions accepted by an
                    active ruling are logged to stderr and do not fail).
        motion      Screen still swapping frames under reduced motion.
        load        Host failed to load or place the screen.
        warning     Qt or theme-engine runtime warning while shown.
        stopped     Audit pass halted (for example, a view still moving
                    after 5 s).
        recording   Captured screenshot dimensions do not match the
                    requested window size.
        mockup      With --mockups, element geometry, colour, or words
                    differ from the mockup spec beyond tolerance.

    By default theme-audit runs offscreen on the software renderer with
    QSG_RENDER_LOOP=basic. Audited screen counts are printed to stderr
    as 'theme-audit: held <Screen> in <N> states...'.

OPTIONS
    --static
        (theme-check) Run only the static check without launching
        theme-audit.
    --state DIR
        Record each audited state as Screen-variant-WxH.spec and .png
        under DIR (or DIR/<package> when checking multiple folders).
    --gpu
        (theme-audit) Render with Vulkan inside a dedicated virtual
        Wayland compositor (kwin_wayland --virtual at 3840x2160, scale
        1) so shader effects such as masks and blurs are drawn.
    --states LIST
        (theme-audit) Comma-separated list of states from STATES below,
        or 'all' (default: default).
    --list-states
        (theme-audit) Print all supported states as tab-separated
        'name, screens, description' rows and exit.
    --sizes LIST
        (theme-audit) Comma-separated subset of gate sizes (for example
        '1280x800,3840x2160'), or 'all' (default: all).
    --crowd with|without|only
        (theme-audit) Control the 120-console crowd pass on Consoles in
        the dark variant: run with other passes (default), skip it, or
        run it alone. The crowd pass runs across all sizes in one sweep
        because each size starts where the previous sweep left focus.
    --catalogue FILE
        (theme-audit) Audit Consoles alone against a tab-separated
        catalogue file (maker, name, count, optional engine, kind, look;
        '#' comments), labelling states by FILE's stem.
    --section KEY
        (theme-audit) Console or shelf key to show on the Games screen.
    --focus NAME
        (theme-audit, with --catalogue) Move initial focus to the
        console named NAME before judging each size.
    --mockups DIR
        (theme-audit) Compare default dark screens at 1280x800 and
        1920x1200 against <package>-<Screen>.mockup.spec files in DIR.

STATES
    Each state feeds EmuSen.Theme surfaces (Library, Browse, Session,
    Device, Tokens) through the host without modifying theme files.
    Recordings include the state name (for example
    Home-dark-nogame-1280x800). The synthetic default library contains
    eight games with generated covers across four consoles, one
    suspended NES game, one controller, clock 21:42, and 64% battery.

    default     the synthetic library with Fable of Tiles suspended;
                the splash finished under reduced motion; Choose a
                console again over 120 consoles; Settings on its
                Display page, its first row focused
    nogame      Home with no game to continue
    empty       Home, Consoles, and Games over empty.tsv (no consoles
                or games; Games shows the All shelf)
    one-console the synthetic library's NES games alone, one suspended
    one-game    Games over one-game.tsv (a console holding one game)
    many        Games over many.tsv (a console holding 9,000 games)
    nocover     the default library with no covers
    norecent    the same games never played and none hearted, no game
                suspended
    long        a ninth game with an extra-long title, played last and
                suspended
    pressed     Return held on the first focus while judged and recorded
    disabled    Home with Scraper declined by the host and focused via
                the pad walk
    loud        Home with navigation sound at full volume (longest
                Settings subtitle)
    splash-1s   Splash with motion allowed and animation clock held at
                1 s after placement
    splash-3s   Splash with animation clock held at 3 s
    splash-5s   Splash with animation clock held at 5 s

    Held-clock states advance a custom 16 ms-per-frame animation driver
    without waiting for rest; QML Timers are not controlled by the
    animation clock.

EXIT STATUS
    0   No findings.
    1   One or more findings reported.
    2   Invalid options, missing folder, theme-audit not found (without
        --static), or runtime setup failure.

ENVIRONMENT
    EMUSEN_THEME_AUDIT
        Path to the theme-audit executable when not on PATH.
    EMUSEN_PLATFORM_LIBRARY, EMUSEN_TEST_CORE
        Prebuilt platform library and test core for the synthetic
        library (built via cargo if unset).

EXAMPLES
    theme-check Frontend/themes/emusen
    theme-check --static Frontend/themes/emusen
    theme-check --state /tmp/eclipse Frontend/themes/eclipse
    theme-audit --gpu --state /tmp/eclipse-gpu Frontend/themes/eclipse
    theme-audit --states all --state /tmp/states Frontend/themes/eclipse
    theme-audit --states nogame,splash-3s Frontend/themes/eclipse
    theme-audit --sizes 1920x1080 --crowd without Frontend/themes/eclipse
    theme-audit --catalogue Testing/themes/catalogues/n30.tsv Frontend/themes/emusen

SEE ALSO
    qml-rules(1), esde-check(1), dupes(1)
